		"help.close": "Close",
		"help.resources": "Elixir and hand\n• Deploying units, attaching parasites and casting spells costs the card's Elixir cost.\n• A normal turn restores %d Elixir and draws %d cards. Player 2's first turn grants %d Elixir and draws %d cards.\n• A normal attack that kills an enemy unit refunds 1 Elixir. Skill kills have no automatic refund.\n• Dragging a hand or board card into the discard pile refunds 1 Elixir. Gains are capped by maximum Elixir.\n• Hand limit: %d cards. An empty deck is refilled from the shuffled discard pile.",
		"help.actions": "Action Points (this match)\n• After start-of-turn skills and draws: AP = %s + %s × empty board slots + %s × empty hand slots, rounded down with a minimum of 0. Changing empty slots during the turn does not refresh AP.\n• Normal attacks and active skills share one army-wide action count: the first is free, then costs rise to 1, 2, 3… AP.\n• Spend remaining AP first. The shortage × %s is paid in Elixir, rounded up. Insufficient resources prevent the action.\n• Deployment, spells, summon skills and passive triggers do not advance the action count.",
		"help.actions_legacy": "Action Points (legacy match)\n• Unit actions cost no AP or additional Elixir in this match. Card deployment costs still apply.\n• Unit and skill use limits still apply.",
		"help.skills": "Units and skills\n• Each unit may make one normal attack per turn. Attacking prevents active skills; using an active skill prevents a normal attack.\n• Different active skills may be used consecutively. Each active skill can be used once per turn, subject to resources and its total use limit.\n• Summon skills resolve on deployment, prompting for a target when needed. Passives trigger by their card conditions and cost no AP.\n• Total use limits persist across turns until the card is reset. Each parasite tracks its own uses.\n• Silence disables all skills, including passives and talents, but allows basic attacks. Stun also blocks basic attacks until the end of the next friendly turn. The unit stays on board, takes damage and protects its player.",
		"help.combat": "Combat and ending a turn\n• %s\n• To attack, select a friendly unit and then an enemy unit. Normal attacks must prioritize enemy Taunt units.\n• Temporary Elixir expires first when ending a turn, before end-of-turn effects.\n• From round 2, if the enemy has no living units, unused units attack the hero automatically from left to right, paying action resources.\n• Hover over End Turn or hold it on a touchscreen to preview damage and costs. Skills and statuses during resolution may change the result.",
