		"tutorial.title_battle_title": "Find a match here",
		"tutorial.title_battle_body": "%s offers local practice, online play, the tutorial and action challenges. Practice against the computer before facing other players. You can replay the tutorial here.",
		"tutorial.title_create_title": "Create your first card",
		"tutorial.title_create_body": "%s sets a card's name, cost, health, attack and skills. Next, use the real editors and battlefield. An unfinished first tutorial restarts on the next launch; skipping stops automatic guidance.",
		"tutorial.title_begin": "Create Your First Card",
		"tutorial.intro_body": "Learn the board, then summon your created card, attack, and pass the turn. Only the actions for each step are open. You can skip or exit at any time.",
		"tutorial.hud_title": "Read the Battlefield",
		"tutorial.hud_body": "Your opponent is above; you are below. Red bars show player Health, separate from unit HP. Reduce the opponent's Health to 0 to win. You lose when your own Health reaches 0.",
		"tutorial.board_title": "Five Slots on Each Side",
		"tutorial.board_body": "The upper red slots belong to the opponent; the lower blue slots are yours. Each slot holds one unit. Cards in your hand are not on the board: deploy units into your empty slots to fight.",
		"tutorial.hand_title": "Hand, Shared Deck, and Discard",
		"tutorial.hand_body": "Your hand is below, with a limit of %d cards. Both players draw from the shared deck on the left. Drag unwanted hand cards or units to the discard pile on the right to gain 1 Elixir, up to the cap. An empty deck reshuffles the discard pile.",
		"tutorial.resources_title": "Elixir and Action Points",
		"tutorial.resources_body": "Blue Elixir pays card costs; gold AP pays for attacks and active skills. Deployment, spells, summon skills, and passives do not increase the action count. When AP runs out, Elixir covers the shortage. You cannot act without enough resources.",
		"tutorial.actions_title": "Your Army Shares Action Costs",
		"tutorial.actions_body": "After start skills and draws resolve, AP = %s + %s × empty board slots + %s × empty hand slots, rounded down and fixed for the turn. Army-wide attacks and actives cost 0, 1, 2... Pay AP first, then shortage × %s in Elixir, rounded up. A unit can attack OR use actives; different unused actives can chain.",
		"tutorial.actions_legacy_body": "This legacy position has no AP costs. A unit may attack once per turn OR use different unused active skills. Attacking blocks its actives; using an active blocks its attack.",
		"tutorial.summon_title": "Summon a Card",
		"tutorial.summon_body": "Cost: %d Elixir; you have %d. Drag this card to your glowing center slot. Deployment pays its card cost, without spending AP or increasing the action count.",
		"tutorial.skill_title": "Summon Skills Resolve Automatically",
		"tutorial.skill_body": "On Summon resolved on entry without using an attack or active action. Draw effects add deck cards to your hand; targeted summon skills ask for a target immediately.",
		"tutorial.stats_title": "Card Cost, HP, and ATK",
		"tutorial.stats_body": "This unit has Cost %d, current HP %d, and ATK %d. Cost is paid when deploying from hand. HP keeps the unit alive; ATK determines normal attack damage. Unit HP is separate from player Health.",
		"tutorial.attack_title": "Start a Basic Attack",
		"tutorial.attack_body": "Click your unit to open its details, press Attack there, then choose an enemy unit. Training allows round-one attacks; ordinary matches normally forbid them. Check the match rules.",
		"tutorial.target_title": "Choose the Target",
		"tutorial.target_body": "Click the glowing Training Dummy above. Normal damage equals effective ATK; each unit attacks at most once per turn. Manual attacks target units. Player Health is attacked through end-of-turn conditions.",
		"tutorial.result_title": "Read the Actual Result",
		"tutorial.result_body": "Dummy HP %d → %d. This attack paid %d AP and %d Elixir; the next army action requires %d. A unit leaves at 0 HP. Normal-attack kills refund 1 Elixir; skill kills give no automatic refund.",
		"tutorial.face_title": "How to Hit Player Health",
